WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.609
The Guardians of the Galaxy are gearing up
for one last ride in the MCU.

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:07.890
Will critics pump the brakes on this blaze
of glory?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.170
So far, the reactions have been largely positive,
though some have a few complaints.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:16.530
After a complicated production history, "Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3."

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:21.840
finally hits theaters on May 5, 2023, bringing
director James Gunn's Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:27.320
space opera to a heartstring-tugging conclusion
that centers around the extremely tragic backstory

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.859
of Bradley Cooper's Rocket.

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:34.950
"Me and my friends are gonna go flyin' together,
into the forever and beautiful sky."

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:39.130
Now that some people have already been able
to see the movie a little early, eagerly-awaited

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.559
first reactions have started to arrive.

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:45.739
Fortunately for fans of the series, many of
these first impressions are nothing short

00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:46.739
of stellar.

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:49.790
But there are also those who have spotted
some strain at the seams.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:54.180
Steven Weintraub of Collider was among those
enamored by the film, praising the experience

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:56.699
of seeing the movie in IMAX and tweeting,

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:58.340
"Loved #GuardiansOfTheGalaxyVol3.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:03.290
@JamesGunn is leaving Marvel with an exceptional
last film and it's loaded with so many great

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.439
moments it's hard to pick my favorite scene."

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:09.630
Verge's Charles Pulliam was somewhat more
critical, finding that the film leaned a bit

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.340
too much on the wrong things.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.340
He tweeted,

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:16.750
"Guardians of the Galaxy 3's very pretty,
too jokey, and hinges on you still being wrapped

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.890
up in the emotional fervor of Endgame, which
I don't think a lot of people are."

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.960
"Her dad threw her off a magic cliff and she
died, and then I lost my temper and nearly

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.270
destroyed half the universe."

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:29.530
A lot of people who have seen the movie early
do seem to have that emotional fervor, though.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:34.030
Gunn's final work for the MCU has been a long
time coming, and more than one first reaction

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:38.780
specifically advised the viewer to bring tissues
because of the sheer emotional impact.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.360
For example, Leo Rydel of Geekly Goods enthused
on Twitter,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.310
"Emotional, action packed, comedic, and a
tone that delivers.

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:49.830
GRAB THE TISSUES cause DAMN there are some
MOMENTS man!!

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:50.830
Rocket is the MAN!!

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.860
Music choices Great per usual and VFX deliver!

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.119
HAD A BLAST!"

00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:58.439
Andrew J. Salazar of Discussing Film agreed,
tweeting,

00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:03.240
"#GuardiansOfTheGalaxyVol3 has the most heart
&amp; soul from any MCU film in a long time.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.624
At times it's hard to believe that Gunn got
away with so much of this, in the best way possible.

00:02:07.624 --> 00:02:10.920
You're going to need tissues, but not for
the reasons you're expecting."

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:16.330
Several others, like Mike Ryan of Uproxx and
Sean Tajipour of Nerdtropolis, also praised

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:21.670
the movie and the emotional punch it packs,
while Pop Cult Planet and MTV's Kristen Maldonado

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:25.239
credited "Vol. 3" for breathing new life in
the genre, tweeting,

00:02:25.239 --> 00:02:31.870
"After so much superhero movie fatigue, #GuardiansOfTheGalaxyVol3
is a refreshing &amp; unexpected joy to watch."

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:36.269
Even the critical first impressions that weren't
entirely praise seem to be mostly positive

00:02:36.269 --> 00:02:41.250
about the film, pointing out individual issues
rather than outright lambasting "Vol. 3" as

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.250
a whole.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.269
Hoai-Tran Bui of Inverse saw good things in
the movie, but lamented its apparent lack

00:02:46.269 --> 00:02:48.370
of stakes in the grander scheme of things.

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:49.370
She tweeted,

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:54.010
"GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY VOL. 3 is the STAR
TREK BEYOND of the series, in the best and

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.190
not-so-best ways.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:59.360
But Gunn is really good at this whole disarmingly
earnest superhero thing, and even more so

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.760
when he unleashes his old Troma instincts.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.730
Wish it felt less like a side quest tho."

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:05.690
"We're listening to everything you're saying."

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:07.940
"And it is painful."

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:11.799
Alex Madden, who reviews films on YouTube,
felt the movie couldn't quite deliver on the

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:18.020
level the very first "Guardians of the Galaxy"
did, but still rated it above "Vol. 2.," tweeting,

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.379
"#GuardiansOfTheGalaxyVol3 takes a lot of
big swings and mostly delivers.

00:03:21.379 --> 00:03:26.139
A couple hiccups here and there but the glue
that holds this movie together is definitely Rocket."

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.440
Meanwhile, Matt Neglia of Next Best Picture
took a harsher approach.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.590
He praised the visuals, but said the rest
was a mixed bag, tweeting,

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:39.561
"GUARDIANS OF THE GALAXY VOL. 3 aspires for
sweeping emotion, gut busting laughs &amp; thrilling action.

00:03:39.561 --> 00:03:44.269
It sometimes succeeds but as a send off for
all of these characters, it feels strangely

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:46.489
uneven &amp; anticlimactic."

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:51.110
It seems that the people who enjoyed seeing
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" love it very,

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:55.470
very much, and even the ones who weren't quite
so swept away with it found plenty of good

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:56.950
to go with the bad.

